1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,284
This is the Orient Cables (India) I P O, a mainboard offer,

2
00:00:04,284 --> 00:00:08,640
open from the twenty-fifth to the twenty-ninth of September.

3
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:12,172
The price band is ₹258 to ₹272.

4
00:00:12,172 --> 00:00:18,138
Every figure here comes from the final red herring prospectus

5
00:00:18,138 --> 00:00:20,192
and exchange notices;

6
00:00:20,192 --> 00:00:24,006
the final price is fixed after bidding,

7
00:00:24,006 --> 00:00:28,212
so valuations are computed at the ₹272 cap.

8
00:00:28,712 --> 00:00:29,949
First, the business.

9
00:00:30,449 --> 00:00:33,351
Orient Cables makes networking cables,

10
00:00:33,351 --> 00:00:36,786
the LAN cables inside offices and data rooms,

11
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:38,924
plus specialty power cables,

12
00:00:38,924 --> 00:00:42,055
optical-fibre cables and cable harnesses,

13
00:00:42,055 --> 00:00:44,956
including E V charging-gun assemblies.

14
00:00:45,456 --> 00:00:50,977
The RHP's industry report puts it among India's top four

15
00:00:50,977 --> 00:00:53,344
networking-cable makers,

16
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:56,400
with about 22.9% share in FY26.

17
00:00:56,900 --> 00:01:00,456
It runs two plants in Bhiwadi, Rajasthan,

18
00:01:00,456 --> 00:01:04,879
and a new Bengaluru plant that started in May 2026.

19
00:01:05,379 --> 00:01:06,979
The financial checkpoint.

20
00:01:07,479 --> 00:01:19,884
FY26 revenue was ₹1,171.65 Cr, against ₹824.96 Cr in FY25,

21
00:01:19,884 --> 00:01:23,948
a change of 42.03%.

22
00:01:24,448 --> 00:01:31,744
Profit after tax was ₹53.81 Cr, a margin of 4.59%.

23
00:01:32,244 --> 00:01:33,247
Here is the catch.

24
00:01:33,747 --> 00:01:40,792
Revenue grew 42.03%, but profit barely moved,

25
00:01:40,792 --> 00:01:45,176
from ₹53.32 Cr to ₹53.81 Cr,

26
00:01:45,176 --> 00:01:51,283
so the margin fell from 6.46% to 4.59%.

27
00:01:51,783 --> 00:01:56,040
The June 2026 quarter looked stronger:

28
00:01:56,040 --> 00:02:01,194
₹489.16 Cr of revenue and ₹33.22 Cr of profit,

29
00:02:01,194 --> 00:02:06,012
though a single quarter is not a full year.

30
00:02:06,512 --> 00:02:10,864
The offer size at the cap is ₹552.00 Cr.

31
00:02:11,364 --> 00:02:16,190
₹320.00 Cr is fresh issue that goes into the company,

32
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:22,564
and ₹232.00 Cr is an offer for sale that goes to selling shareholders.

33
00:02:23,064 --> 00:02:27,524
So 57.97% of the deal is new capital,

34
00:02:27,524 --> 00:02:32,707
and 42.03% is an exit for existing holders.

35
00:02:33,207 --> 00:02:34,529
Where does the money go?

36
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:43,349
Of the ₹320.00 Cr fresh issue, ₹155.50 Cr repays debt.

37
00:02:43,849 --> 00:02:48,208
₹91.50 Cr goes to machinery and civil works,

38
00:02:48,208 --> 00:02:52,468
and the rest to general corporate purposes.

39
00:02:52,968 --> 00:03:00,037
The ₹232.00 Cr offer for sale goes to the promoter family and its two trusts,

40
00:03:00,037 --> 00:03:07,197
whose average acquisition cost the ad lists as between zero and ₹0.01 a share.

41
00:03:07,697 --> 00:03:09,063
Now, valuation.

42
00:03:09,563 --> 00:03:12,105
At the ₹272 cap,

43
00:03:12,105 --> 00:03:20,528
the price is 51.61x FY26 earnings per share of ₹5.27.

44
00:03:21,028 --> 00:03:28,361
That sits near the top of its listed cable peers:

45
00:03:28,361 --> 00:03:35,844
Finolex at 26.29x, Havells 42.69x, Polycab 46.69x,

46
00:03:35,844 --> 00:03:40,633
KEI 48.99x and R R Kabel 54.85x.

47
00:03:41,133 --> 00:03:47,658
The RHP's 128.11x industry average is pulled up by Sterlite

48
00:03:47,658 --> 00:03:50,312
Technologies at 708.38x,

49
00:03:50,312 --> 00:03:54,957
so the peer range is the fairer yardstick.

50
00:03:55,457 --> 00:03:56,951
Now balance the evidence.

51
00:03:57,451 --> 00:03:58,589
Watch-out:

52
00:03:58,589 --> 00:04:02,574
PAT flat while revenue grew 42.03%.

53
00:04:02,574 --> 00:04:03,598
Strength:

54
00:04:03,598 --> 00:04:09,632
About 22.9% share of India's networking-cable market.

55
00:04:10,132 --> 00:04:11,560
Watch-out:

56
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:17,413
51.61x P/E, near the top of listed peers.

57
00:04:17,413 --> 00:04:18,698
Strength:

58
00:04:18,698 --> 00:04:20,840
Strong Q1 FY27:

59
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:24,980
₹33.22 Cr PAT in one quarter.

60
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,884
Watch-out:

61
00:04:26,884 --> 00:04:31,940
42.03% of the offer is promoter OFS.

62
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:33,203
Strength:

63
00:04:33,203 --> 00:04:38,259
₹155.50 Cr of fresh money cuts debt.

64
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:39,889
How to apply.

65
00:04:40,389 --> 00:04:44,832
The minimum bid is one lot of 55 shares,

66
00:04:44,832 --> 00:04:47,941
which is ₹14,960 at the cap.

67
00:04:48,441 --> 00:04:51,917
Retail investors can bid up to two lakh rupees,

68
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:56,057
and allotment is by lottery if retail is oversubscribed.

69
00:04:56,557 --> 00:05:01,100
Check live subscription on the N S E or B S E website,

70
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,531
not social media.

71
00:05:03,031 --> 00:05:03,991
Let's recap.

72
00:05:04,491 --> 00:05:10,703
FY26 revenue ₹1,171.65 Cr, profit ₹53.81 Cr.

73
00:05:10,703 --> 00:05:19,599
The offer is ₹552.00 Cr, of which ₹232.00 Cr is offer for sale.

74
00:05:19,599 --> 00:05:25,247
Valuation is 51.61x earnings at the cap.

75
00:05:25,247 --> 00:05:30,048
The minimum investment is ₹14,960.

76
00:05:30,548 --> 00:05:34,722
This video is public-source education from the red herring

77
00:05:34,722 --> 00:05:37,024
prospectus and exchange notices.

78
00:05:37,024 --> 00:05:40,982
It is not investment advice and not a buy or sell call.

79
00:05:40,982 --> 00:05:42,781
Read the final documents,

80
00:05:42,781 --> 00:05:45,660
check live subscription on the exchange,

81
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:48,394
and consult a SEBI-registered adviser.

82
00:05:48,394 --> 00:05:49,833
Thanks for watching.

